# The six standalone page names have been shared and bookmarked. They must keep
# working, and they must keep their ADDRESS: the router reads the page name out
# of the URL to know which course was asked for, so these are rewrites (200),
# never redirects (301). A redirect would strip the very thing being read.
#
# tools/check-links.mjs asserts all six, plus the query grammar they carry, and
# tools/serve.mjs reproduces this rule locally so the legacy half is exercised
# for real rather than assumed.
/veckefjarden3d.html    /index.html   200
/norrfallsviken3d.html  /index.html   200
/puttom3d.html          /index.html   200
/angso3d.html           /index.html   200
/upsala3d.html          /index.html   200
/johannesberg3d.html    /index.html   200

# There is deliberately NO /* catch-all. The app has no path routes -- a course
# is chosen with ?bana=, the view with the rest of the query -- so everything
# outside the six names above is a real static file, and a catch-all would only
# serve HTML in place of one that is missing. A pack fetched as an HTML page
# fails on its GPK1 magic instead of on an honest 404, which is a worse hour to
# spend. tools/serve.mjs makes the same choice, and says so.
